HSE06 checks (2026-09-29)

Purpose
1. HSE06 band gap and band edges of 2H-alpha (a-Beryllene_hh), the only insulator (PBE indirect gap 4.84 eV).
2. Band order and inversion parities at the four TRIM under HSE06 for the conditional Fu-Kane indices
   (critical case: 2H-beta at M, where the pair above band 6 has the opposite parity and lies only 0.177 eV higher in PBE).

Cost-saving choices
- No SOC: Be/H spin-orbit splittings are about 1 meV, and inversion acts on the spatial part only, so spinless parities
  equal the Kramers-pair parities.
- 20 A cell instead of 40 A (slab <= 3.8 A thick, centred at z = 0.5, DIPOL 0.5 0.5 0.5): about 2-4x cheaper.
- Each job first runs PBE in the same cell (reference, and the starting WAVECAR), then HSE06 (ISTART = 1, ALGO = Damped).
- Accuracy is not reduced to save time (revised 2026-09-29 at the user's request): full 12x12 exchange q mesh (no NKRED),
  PRECFOCK = Normal. The in-job PBE step in the 20 A cell is compared with the 40 A / 105x105 PBE eigenvalues at the TRIM
  to quantify the vacuum and k-mesh effect; the mesh is increased if that difference is not negligible.
- scf/: Gamma-centred 12x12 k mesh (contains all four TRIM).
- 2H-alpha band structure split into 10 independent jobs of <= 10 zero-weight points each, on top of the weighted IBZ of the
  12x12 mesh (43 points): Gamma-K 30, K-M 15, M-Gamma 26 points (proportional to segment length), plus 9 points around the
  PBE VBM (0.2546, 0.2546) and 9 around the CBM (0.4268, 0).

Outputs: *.pbe files = PBE step, plain OUTCAR/EIGENVAL/vasprun.xml = HSE06 step. Parities at the TRIM come from IrRep
on the HSE06 WAVECAR (non-spinor).

Results (2026-10-01; jobs 43630-43644 all exit 0, SCF converged in 12-21 steps)
- Parities (scf/hse_parity.json, 9.0_topology/tools/hse_parity.py): identical to PBE+SOC at all four TRIM for all five
  structures; conditional nu unchanged. 2H-beta gap above band 6 at M: 0.171 eV (HSE06) vs 0.178 eV (PBE, same cell).
  ST: the N = 6 boundary at M lies inside an orbital doublet of single parity, split only by SOC.
- In-job PBE (20 A, 12x12) vs 40 A / 105x105 PBE+SOC TRIM gaps: <= 1 meV (2H-alpha), <= 8 meV (beta, ST, 2H-beta),
  65 meV (alpha, gaps > 5 eV). No denser mesh or larger vacuum needed.
- 2H-alpha: HSE06 indirect gap 5.998 eV (PBE 4.842 eV), direct 6.089 eV; VBM (0.2546, 0.2546), CBM (0.4268, 0) unchanged.
- beta here uses the superseded P-1 geometry (see 2.0_geometry_optimization/b-Beryllene_p3m1/note).
Details: 9.0_topology/docs/topo_report_20261001.md, Section 2.
